const s = section('typing', 'Typing',
  'This section introduces the typing judgment $\\Gamma ; \\Delta \\vdash^{F} e : T \\ ! \\ \\varepsilon$, its contexts $\\Gamma$ and $\\Delta$ and the future $F$ with the update $F \\triangleleft H$ for what is held, the side conditions on points, aging $T - c$ and capture of credits, subtyping, one rule per term former, the process judgment $\\Sigma \\vdash^{N}_{W} p : T$ with the rules P-Term and P-Connect, the lock-free judgment $\\Sigma \\Vdash^{N}_{W} p : T$, and the guard $\\Lambda \\vdash\\!\\triangleright t$. Deadlock-free typing is the instance $N = \\infty$ with every annotation erased, and lock-free typing takes $N \\in \\mathbb{N}$ and adds the guard.');

